# Banter in Wickermoor Village (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is wickermoor): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ wickermoor_village_01_silas_delphine_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:wickermoor_village and not flag.vessla_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the mugs carved into that oak, Delphine, every one of 'em pulling a worse poker face than the faceless gent across the mud.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: At least the Founder's statue knows how to hold a pose, darling, though billing yourself without a nose is a bold choice for the square.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The storm drives the damp right down from that crooked estate, and Dreadfang does not care for the spoor round the roots.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell's in the twitch, friend, and when a whole village carves its worries into tree bark instead of skipping town, the house already owns the deed.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then let them keep their soggy bark, Silas, because my hem is taking on water and I refuse to play to an empty square.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_green_queen_inn_02_tobin_rook_cordelia
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:wickermoor_green_queen_inn and not flag.vessla_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Three paces back from the taproom hearth, Rook, the grease on those kitchen counters would take a spark quicker than dry clover.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Chimney draw is sluggish, Tobin, and that board of rumours by the bar hasn't been cleared by a proper clerk in six months.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Never mind the hearth, darling, the tallow smoke and warm ale are doing fascinating things to every pulse in this room.
interject name:tobin_hayward: They are stewing in their own damp, Cordelia, and half the timber round that little stage has rot behind the wainscot.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Settle down now, the roof holds the rain off, and a dry ledger by the bar is more than we had on the moor.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_village_03_silas_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:cordelia_skein and at:wickermoor_village and flag.vessla_slain and not flag.act2_done
interject name:silas_vane: Funny how quiet the square goes once the sky stops spitting, Cordelia, you can actually hear that clocktower ticking over the river.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The barometric drop has eased, darling, and the villagers' heartbeats have slowed by a full third since the clouds broke over the hill.
interject name:silas_vane: You call it pulse ratios, I call it folks stepping out by the well without checking if the roof's about to fold on 'em.
interject name:cordelia_skein: It is a remarkably resilient little specimen of a town, Silas, even if Old Rusty by the pavilion smells entirely of wet iron.
interject name:silas_vane: Give 'em an hour in the dry, friend, and somebody will be running a three-card shoe off the Founder's plinth.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_shop_bakery_04_silas_rook
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and at:wickermoor_shop_bakery and flag.act2_done >= 2
interject name:silas_vane: Best spot in the hollow, Rook, warm flour in the air and not a single thing on those cooling racks trying to bite my fingers off.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Oven brickwork is sound and the sacks are stacked clear of the damp, though this warmth isn't doing my knuckles any favours, Silas.
interject name:silas_vane: Right, forgot you frostbitten lads don't care for a snug bakehouse, I can shift my censer by the door if the heat's crowding you.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Leave it be, lad, the yeast and warm flour beat cellar mould, even if I can't recall the last time I ate a loaf.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_village_05_delphine_rook
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:rook_coldwake and at:wickermoor_village and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at The Green Queen's sign swinging in the dark, Rook, it feels like the whole square could fit inside a hatbox tonight.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Small parish, Delphine, doesn't take long to learn where the roots lift the cobbles by the oak or which roofs leak.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness hasn't made a single crack since we passed the well, and I think I might actually miss this muddy little stage when the curtain falls.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Slabs are level and the folk know our names now, so we'll see the shift through properly before we pack the ledger.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Mind the seams, darling, you are going to make me sound sentimental in front of the turnip over that door.
endif
-> END

~ rk_dovecote_r1_06_lucan_rook
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:rook_coldwake and at:rk_dovecote_r1 and flag.rk_started and not flag.golub_dead
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Rook, the moor is moving past that round window, and Barnaby is tucked so tight against my boots I can scarcely step.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Complete violation of parish zoning, Lucan, a building has no business strolling across the turf with this many undelivered letters in storage.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The cooing from the roost above is deafening, if you please, and some magpie has woven a whole nest of stolen ribbon beside the seed sacks.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unruly administration from cellar to rafters, and if that ladder isn't pegged to regulation, we'll be citing the keeper in person.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Stay close by the leather cord, good boy, it is only floorboards groaning, not thunder.
endif
-> END

~ fd_festival_07_tobin_delphine
if name:tobin_hayward and name:delphine_ravelle and at:fd_festival and flag.festival_active and not flag.chuckles_dead
interject name:tobin_hayward: That building is packed to the rafters with hand pies and scotch eggs, Delphine, the crust is sweating right through the lath and plaster.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Never mind the pastry, Tobin, look at the cheap seats out here, ribbons strung roof to roof and a clown balloon the size of a cart.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep between me and that bonfire in the square, the dancers are shoving too close and the whole street smells of hot suet.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Take my elbow, I know how a rigged house works when the music won't stop, and we are not staying for the encore.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good soil, bad seed, and whatever stretched these lanes three times wide needs weeding at the taproot.
endif
-> END

~ fd_silent_church_08_tobin_rook
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and at:fd_silent_church and flag.festival_active and not flag.chuckles_dead
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hear that, Rook, the horns and drums cut off right at the threshold like someone took shears to a briar.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Good thick stone, Tobin, even with tarps over the windows, and the new timber round the altar is laid square.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Sweet resin in the boards too, fresh pine, not a speck of festival rot or bonfire smoke on the air in here.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Could do without the marble lad sneering at the door, mind, twice regulation height and blocking the main aisle.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Let him sneer, so long as he keeps the sparks and the dancers on the other side of the step.
endif
-> END
